<title>JAPAN: Seibu Oil's 120,000 bpd topper resumes operations.</title>
<headline>Seibu Oil's 120,000 bpd topper resumes operations.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seibu Oil Co Ltd, a Showa Shell Sekiyu KK group refiner, said it restarted its 120,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit at its Yamaguchi plant in western Japan on Friday morning.</p>
<p>The unit had been shut since August 29 for routine maintenance checks.</p>
<p>Showa Shell Sekiyu KK, an oil refiner and distributor, is owned 50 percent by the Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
